--- Architecture ---
Self-contained SwiftUI surface bound through one @Observable DrivingDynamicsPageModel
+ a DrivingDynamicsSource seam (InMemoryDrivingDynamicsSource for previews/tests),
Foundation+SwiftUI+Charts only (no `import Shared`; the production source is wired at
integration, like every sibling surface). Pure Foundation projector ports the web
derivations (computeMotorStats, speed buckets, accel scatter, power profile, coach
style breakdown, tips) with SI->display conversion at the render boundary
(unitConversion.ts `*FromSI`). All 11 web sections reproduced in render order:
LiveMotorStatus, GForcePanel, PedalUsage, SpeedGearPanel, AutopilotSection,
MotorHistoryCharts, MotorEfficiencyInsights, SummaryStats, DrivingCoachSection,
DriveAnalyticsSection (with functional date-range filter), DrivingTips. Charts use
native Swift Charts; gauges/cards use the P3 token components (TSGlassPanel,
TSStatCard, TSMetricBar, TSEmptyState, TSSkeleton, TSFadeIn); colors/typography via
the P2 Color.TS / Font.TS tokens; every visible string via the P1/S10 facade.

